{{Quote|There's an ocean planet&hellip; home to Nautolans. Glee Anselm?|[[Mace Windu]]|audio=HomeOfNautolans-CotF.flac|<ref name="Children of the Force">{{TCW|Children of the Force}}</ref>}}
'''Glee Anselm''' was an [[Waterworld|ocean planet]] located in the [[Jalor system]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Anselmi]] and [[Nautolan]] [[species]]. [[Star Tours]], a tour company, offered vacation tours of Glee Anselm during the [[Clone Wars]]. During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[senator]]s representing the [[planet]] in the [[Imperial Senate]] were fiercely loyal to the Empire. Glee Anselm was also the homeworld of the criminal [[Tobias Beckett]] and the [[Jedi Master]] [[Kit Fisto]].

==Description==
Glee Anselm was a [[planet]]<ref name="Glee Anselm" /> located in the [[Jalor system]]<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" /> within [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]].<ref name="TFABG" /> The planet's surface was covered in [[water]], and it had no major landmasses.<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" /> No light reached the depths of the world's [[ocean]]s, making the [[Nautolan]] people evolve to have dark [[eye]]s that could see details in the oceans' darkness.<ref name="Light" /> The small islands dotting its [[ocean]]s held [[jungle]]s, [[mountain]]s,<ref name="Billboard" /> [[beach]]es, and [[grass]]y fields.<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" />

==History==
According to legend, Glee Anselm used to have a continent with life until it sank to the seabed thousands of [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Republic Era|fall]] of the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" />

Prior to the start of the [[Clone Wars]], [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] of the [[Jedi Order]] helped to organize a [[Rescue of Yoda|test]] for [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and his [[Padawan]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], which involved the pair searching for him on Glee Anselm.<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" />

In [[3 BBY]], Glee Anselm was one of only forty worlds that still sent representatives to the [[Apprentice Legislature]]. [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of [[Alderaan]] owned a bed made from Glee Anselm hardwoods.<ref name="Princess of Alderaan" />

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|On my home planet of Glee Anselm, there is a large amphibious beast called the wooriid--a slow moving carnivore gifted with massive jaws full of razor-sharp teeth.|Kit Fisto|<ref name="Mace Windu 5" />}}
Glee Anselm was the home to two [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]], the [[Anselmi]] and Nautolan. The Anselmi lived on land while the Nautolans lived in the water. The Anselmi resented their aquatic cousins, whom the Anselmi referred to as "gill heads," and sought to dominate.<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" /> The planet was also inhabited by [[human]]s<ref name="The Official Guide" /> and creatures including [[lizard-gull]]s, [[whale]]s,<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin" /> and the [[wooriid]].<ref name="Mace Windu 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:GleeAnselmAd.jpg|thumb|right|180px|An advert showing Glee Anselm]]
Glee Anselm was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones (novelization)|novelization]] and [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones (junior novelization)|junior novelization]] of [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], which were written by [[R. A. Salvatore]] and [[Patricia C. Wrede]], respectively, and were both released in [[2003]]. The world was confirmed to be [[canon]] in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[Children of the Force]]," in which it was mentioned by Mace Windu and later was shown in [[hologram]] in the ''[[Xanadu Blood]]''{{'s}} [[fuel]] [[computer]].

''The Clone Wars'' team had considered showing Glee Anselm in physical form in the episode: concept art was drawn depicting the Nautolans living in cities on the backs of enormous [[turtle]]s that surface for breath every few centuries.<ref name="Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Four">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Four|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season Four]]</ref>

